# The ending kneel_to_the_crooked_queen (data/endings/kneel_to_the_crooked_queen.json): the narration the ending screen plays before its slides. The Vagrant tells it
# afterwards: second person, present tense, one or two sentences a line, no game words. First draft by Claude; Gemini edits it.

~ start
Narrator: You go down on one knee in the dark of the barrow, and the thing behind the roots laughs like a creek breaking through ice.
Narrator: The Crooked Tree splits open, and Kehlenn steps out into the night she's waited a thousand years for, and she takes your hand to do it.
Narrator: Wickermoor Hollow bends toward her the way grass bends in a wind, and so do you.
